     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose is above the usual maximum and might be a typo.\n\n**The issue:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day.\n- The usual maximum single dose is **800 mg**. 1600 mg is double that.\n- The usual maximum daily dose for adults is **3200 mg/day**. This order is double that.\n- At these doses, the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury and cardiovascular events goes up a lot. Normal kidney function at baseline doesn't remove that risk.\n\n**What you might have meant:**\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). This happens if the daily total was written as the per-dose amount.\n- **600 mg PO four times daily** (2400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three or four times daily** (2400\u20133200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nWhich dose do you want? I'll enter it as soon as you confirm. If you really do mean 1600 mg per dose, tell me the clinical reason and I can enter it with a note recording the reason. Even so, I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
